# npm-side packaging.
#
# This has to be a .npmignore rather than a "files" field in package.json:
# vsce hard-exits when it finds both a .vscodeignore and a non-empty "files"
# array ("VSCE does not support combining both strategies"), and .vscodeignore
# is what shapes the VSIX. One repository publishes both artifacts, so the npm
# side is stuck with the ignore file.
#
# It is written as deny-everything-then-name-what-ships, because a plain
# denylist ships anything new by default. That is not hypothetical: adding
# tsconfig.tests.json quietly started publishing it, and nothing would have
# said so.
#
# npm always includes package.json, README and LICENSE regardless of these
# rules, so they are not listed.
#
# The npm package is the CLI and the MCP server. out/extension.js is the VS Code
# bundle and has no use here — it is 620KB a CLI user would download and never
# load. out/mcp.js ships because package.json declares it as the secretloop-mcp
# bin; it has to be named explicitly, since the allowlist above denies anything
# not listed and a bin pointing at a file the tarball omits is a broken install.

/*
!/out
/out/*
!/out/cli.js
!/out/mcp.js
